A 63-byte key, one past the 62 that `MaxKeyFields = 2` can represent.

The key hash is taken over exactly `MaxKeyFields` limbs of 31 bytes and the parse side
bounded nothing, so the 63rd byte simply vanished. The document parses and every other
key in it reads back normally, so nothing tells the caller that one of its keys is not
the key it wrote -- and two keys agreeing on 62 bytes become one key.

No lie anywhere: an honest prover, an honest witness, and a document the library should
have refused. That is why this attack carries no patch.
